 THERMAL AND RESONACE PARAMETERS                                  7925 1451   24
 S. Mughabghab, BNL, April 2006                                   7925 1451   25
 The thermal capture cross section at 2200 m/s evaluated by the   7925 1451   26
 IAEA-CRP on standards (98.66b)[Ca06] was adopted.                7925 1451   27
 In the resonance region the resonance parameters of the Atlas    7925 1451   28
 of Nutron Resonacnces [Mu06] were adopted up to 2634 eV.         7925 1451   29
 The parameters of the first bound level were slightly modified   7925 1451   30
 to fit the thermal capture cross section of 98.66 b [Ca06]       7925 1451   31
 instead of 98.65 b [Mu06]. The potential scattering radius was   7925 1451   32
 changed to 9.658 fermi to fit thermal scattering cross section   7925 1451   33
 of 7.90+-0.13 b [Mu06].                                          7925 1451   34
 Above 2634 eV scattering widths were obtained from the capture   7925 1451   35
 kernels by assuming an average radiative width of 124 meV and    7925 1451   36
 resonace spins of either 2 or 1.                                 7925 1451   37
                                                                  7925 1451   38
  Calculated thermal cross sections & resonance integrals:        7925 1451   39
      ---------------------------------------------               7925 1451   40
      Reaction       Cross section    Res. integral               7925 1451   41
                        (barn)           (barn)                   7925 1451   42
      Total           1.06550E+02           -                     7925 1451   43
      Elastic         7.90977E+00           -                     7925 1451   44
      Capture         9.86619E+01      1.56935E+03                7925 1451   45
      ---------------------------------------------               7925 1451   46
                                                                  7925 1451   47
 FAST NEUTRON REGION                                              7925 1451   48
 T. Kawano, LANL, Nov. 2005                                       7925 1451   49
