*************** SUMMARY OF ENDF/B-VI EVALUATION ******************7925 1451   69
                                                                  7925 1451   70
   A new evaluation of all neutron and gamma-ray data above the   7925 1451   71
 resonance region is joined with the endf/b-v resolved resonance  7925 1451   72
 region evaluation and with the Version VI standard cross section 7925 1451   73
 for the (n,gamma) reaction below a neutron energy of 2.5 MeV.    7925 1451   74
                                                                  7925 1451   75
*************** GENERAL DESCRIPTION ******************************7925 1451   76
                                                                  7925 1451   77
              P.G.Young and E.D.Arthur                            7925 1451   78
                                                                  7925 1451   79
   the new evaluation for files 3,4,5,12,13,14,15 is based on     7925 1451   80
 statistical theory, hauser-feshbach, preequilibrium calculations 7925 1451   81
 with the comnuc and gnash codes (ref1,2). deformed optical poten-7925 1451   82
 tial of delaroche and ecis coupled-channel code were used to cal-7925 1451   83
 culate neutron transmission coefficients and total and elastic   7925 1451   84
 elastic cross sections (ref3,4). gamma-ray strength functions    7925 1451   85
 were obtained by fitting morgan n,xg data (ref5) at 0.4 and 6.5  7925 1451   86
 mev. calculated results were used for all major reactions except 7925 1451   87
 total cross section. for total, the theoretical cross section    7925 1451   88
 was used as prior in covariance analysis of experimental data    7925 1451   89
 using glucs code (ref6). more details on experimental data used  7925 1451   90
 are given below and in main reference for evaluation (ref 7).    7925 1451   91
                                                                  7925 1451   92
 **************************************************************** 7925 1451   93
                                                                  7925 1451   94
                        STANDARDS COVARIANCES                     7925 1451   95
                                                                  7925 1451   96
 Phase 1 reviewers of the ENDF/B-VI standards cross sections have 7925 1451   97
 expressed the concern that the uncertainties resulting from the  7925 1451   98
 combination of R-matrix and simultaneous evaluations might have  7925 1451   99
 led to uncertainties that are too small.  As a result, the       7925 1451  100
 Standards Subcommittee produced (at the May, 1990 CSEWG meeting) 7925 1451  101
 a set of expanded covariance estimates for the standard cross    7925 1451  102
 section reactions.  These uncertainties are estimates such that  7925 1451  103
 if a modern day experiment were performed on a given standard    7925 1451  104
 cross section using the best techniques, approximately 2/3 of    7925 1451  105
 the results should fall within these expanded uncertainties. The 7925 1451  106
 expanded uncertainties for the Au-197(n,gamma) cross section are 7925 1451  107
 given in the following table and are compared to values from the 7925 1451  108
 combined output of the standards covariance analysis:            7925 1451  109
                                                                  7925 1451  110
    Energy Range    Estimated Uncertainty    Combined Analysis    7925 1451  111
      (keV)              (percent)               (percent)        7925 1451  112
                                                                  7925 1451  113
    2.53E-05                 0.14                   0.14          7925 1451  114
     200 - 500               3.0                    1.31          7925 1451  115
     500 - 1000              3.5                    2.1           7925 1451  116
    1000 - 2500              4.5                    2.0           7925 1451  117
                                                                  7925 1451  118
                                                                  7925 1451  119
